<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN CAMPINE ISSUES PROFIT WARNING.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN CAMPINE ISSUES PROFIT WARNING.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian battery recycling company Campine warned on Friday it would end 1996 in the red after its Sanimet-Machelen SA unit plunged to a 79 million Belgian franc loss.</p>
<p>&quot;By this fact, the consolidated 1996 results of the Campine Group will be negative, although the Sanimet-Machelen loss will not affect the results of (parent company) Campine NV,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>A Campine spokeswoman said it would be publishing group results in the first half of May.</p>
